# sys-gym-pastoria (docs/research/gym-puzzles.md): Pastoria Gym's water and
# buttons. A button (a coord event guarded by its map-local var) presses the prop under the player: the three
# colours' pattern animations play once, then the water moves one unit a tick to 0 (orange), 32 (green) or 64
# (blue) and the plate under the pool takes that height. H/M/L ground lets the player in only at 0/32/64, and
# pool tiles whose height would come from the water collide. The route (a shortest walk over the decomp's
# collision rules) presses orange, green, blue, green, orange, blue; a save round trip at the low water;
# every trainer met on the way battled from where they spot the player; Wake won; leaving and re-entering sets
# green again (the onTransition script).
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_ALAKAZAM 80 platinum:MOVE_PSYCHIC platinum:MOVE_PSYCHO_CUT platinum:MOVE_ZEN_HEADBUTT platinum:MOVE_SHADOW_BALL
party 1 platinum:SPECIES_VENUSAUR 80 platinum:MOVE_ENERGY_BALL platinum:MOVE_SOLAR_BEAM platinum:MOVE_EARTHQUAKE platinum:MOVE_SLUDGE_BOMB
set flag platinum:FLAG_HIDE_PASTORIA_CITY_RIVAL true
set flag platinum:FLAG_HIDE_PASTORIA_CITY_CRASHER_WAKE true
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_PASTORIA_CITY_GYM 13 41 up
until idle
+0 assert state mapFeatures {"kind": "pastoria-gym", "pressedButton": 1}
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_MAP_LOCAL_0x01 0
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_MAP_LOCAL_0x02 1
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_MAP_LOCAL_0x03 0
